# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write logs and handle errors {#write-logs-and-handle-errors}"
msgstr "Tulis log dan tangani error {#write-logs-and-handle-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* <Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Placeholder content\">\n"
"- **Errors from custom workflows.** A managed workflow stores a structured error for a custom workflow only when the workflow calls `send_error()`. If custom workflows get the same top-level handler as Catalog Functions, remove the handler from [Best practice: report errors with send_error()](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error).\n"
"- **Time after cancel.** Confirm how long a job can run after `SIGTERM` before the managed workflow stops it.\n"
"</Admonition> */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up your workflow code to write logs, report errors to your local notebook, and save partial work when a job is canceled. To read these outputs from your local notebook, see [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "Atur kode workflow-mu untuk menulis log, melaporkan error ke notebook lokalmu, dan menyimpan hasil parsial saat job dibatalkan. Untuk membaca output ini dari notebook lokalmu, lihat [Jalankan managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| In the workflow | In your local notebook |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Write with a logger from the `logging` module, or call `print()`. | `job.logs()` returns the lines. |\n"
"| Raise an exception, or exit with a nonzero code. | `job.status()` returns `ERROR`, and `job.logs()` shows the traceback. |\n"
"| Call `send_error()`. | `job.error_message()` and `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` return the code, message, and details. |\n"
"| Call `save_result()` in a `SIGTERM` handler. | `job.result()` returns the partial result of a canceled job. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Di workflow | Di notebook lokalmu |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Tulis dengan logger dari modul `logging`, atau panggil `print()`. | `job.logs()` mengembalikan baris-barisnya. |\n"
"| Munculkan exception, atau keluar dengan kode bukan nol. | `job.status()` mengembalikan `ERROR`, dan `job.logs()` menampilkan traceback. |\n"
"| Panggil `send_error()`. | `job.error_message()` dan `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` mengembalikan kode, pesan, dan detail. |\n"
"| Panggil `save_result()` di handler `SIGTERM`. | `job.result()` mengembalikan hasil parsial dari job yang dibatalkan. |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write logs {#write-logs}"
msgstr "Tulis log {#write-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. Read the logs with `job.logs()` while the job runs or after it ends.\n"
msgstr "Apa pun yang ditulis workflow ke standard output atau standard error masuk ke log job. Baca log dengan `job.logs()` saat job berjalan atau setelah selesai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up a logger {#set-up-a-logger}"
msgstr "Siapkan logger {#set-up-a-logger}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the `logging` module from the Python standard library. `logging.basicConfig()` writes to standard error, which reaches the logs without delay. The format in the following example adds a timestamp to each line:\n"
msgstr "Gunakan modul `logging` dari pustaka standar Python. `logging.basicConfig()` menulis ke standard error, yang sampai ke log tanpa tertunda. Format pada contoh berikut menambahkan timestamp ke setiap baris:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`level=logging.WARNING` hides `INFO` messages from other packages, and `logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)` keeps `INFO` messages for your own logger. `qiskit_ibm_runtime` sets its own level with the `QISKIT_IBM_RUNTIME_LOG_LEVEL` environment variable.\n"
msgstr "`level=logging.WARNING` menyembunyikan pesan `INFO` dari paket lain, dan `logger.setLevel(logging.INFO)` mempertahankan pesan `INFO` untuk logger milikmu sendiri. `qiskit_ibm_runtime` mengatur levelnya sendiri dengan environment variable `QISKIT_IBM_RUNTIME_LOG_LEVEL`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`print()` also reaches the logs, but standard output is buffered, so printed lines might not appear until the job ends. If you use `print()`, pass `flush=True`.\n"
msgstr "`print()` juga sampai ke log, tetapi standard output di-buffer, jadi baris yang dicetak mungkin baru muncul setelah job selesai. Kalau kamu memakai `print()`, berikan `flush=True`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: get_logger() from qiskit_serverless adds a [PUBLIC] prefix that Functions uses to split provider and user logs for Catalog Functions; custom workflow logs strip it. Tested with 0.37.0: its lines have no timestamp, and logger.exception() and exc_info=True drop the traceback (PrefixFormatter builds new records with exc_info=None). Confirm whether to recommend the standard logging module for custom workflows, or to fix get_logger(). */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set the log level for each run {#set-the-log-level-for-each-run}"
msgstr "Atur level log untuk setiap run {#set-the-log-level-for-each-run}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To debug one run without changing the code, pass the log level as an argument:\n"
msgstr "Untuk men-debug satu run tanpa mengubah kode, berikan level log sebagai argumen:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, set the level of your logger from the argument:\n"
msgstr "Agar ini berfungsi, atur level logger-mu dari argumen:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow has an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), declare `log_level` in it, for example as `{\"enum\": [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\"]}`.\n"
msgstr "Kalau workflow punya [schema argumen](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), deklarasikan `log_level` di dalamnya, misalnya sebagai `{\"enum\": [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\"]}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: decide what to log {#best-practice-decide-what-to-log}"
msgstr "Praktik terbaik: tentukan apa yang dicatat {#best-practice-decide-what-to-log}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Log enough to reconstruct a run from its logs:\n"
msgstr "Catat cukup banyak agar sebuah run bisa direkonstruksi dari lognya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**At the start, log what the run received.** Log the backend name, the number of circuits, and the other settings that change between runs.\n"
msgstr "**Di awal, catat apa yang diterima run.** Catat nama backend, jumlah circuit, dan pengaturan lain yang berubah antar run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log the start and end of each stage.** Use fixed messages that you can search for.\n"
msgstr "**Catat awal dan akhir setiap tahap.** Pakai pesan tetap yang bisa kamu cari.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log iterations at a fixed interval.** For example, log a line such as `iteration 10/200, energy=-1.1000` every 10 iterations, instead of every iteration.\n"
msgstr "**Catat iterasi pada interval tetap.** Misalnya, catat baris seperti `iteration 10/200, energy=-1.1000` setiap 10 iterasi, bukan setiap iterasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Log exceptions with `logger.exception()` inside an `except` block.** The line includes the full traceback, even if the workflow recovers from the error.\n"
msgstr "**Catat exception dengan `logger.exception()` di dalam blok `except`.** Barisnya menyertakan traceback lengkap, bahkan kalau workflow pulih dari error tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Turn off progress bars.** The logs store each refresh of a progress bar, such as one from `tqdm`, as a separate line. Pass `disable=True` to `tqdm`, or log at an interval instead.\n"
msgstr "**Matikan progress bar.** Log menyimpan setiap refresh progress bar, seperti dari `tqdm`, sebagai baris terpisah. Berikan `disable=True` ke `tqdm`, atau catat pada interval tertentu saja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Keep the logs small.** Do not log large data, such as every shot. A managed workflow keeps only the newest 50 MB of logs for each job.\n"
msgstr "**Jaga log tetap kecil.** Jangan catat data besar, seperti setiap shot. Managed workflow hanya menyimpan 50 MB log terbaru untuk setiap job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Use the words \"error\" and \"exception\" only in messages about failures.** If a failed job did not [report its error](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), the exception that `job.result()` raises contains only the log lines that include these words.\n"
msgstr "**Gunakan kata \"error\" dan \"exception\" hanya dalam pesan tentang kegagalan.** Kalau job yang gagal tidak [melaporkan errornya](#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), exception yang dimunculkan `job.result()` hanya berisi baris log yang memuat kata-kata ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: report errors with send_error() {#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error}"
msgstr "Praktik terbaik: laporkan error dengan send_error() {#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status, and the traceback goes to the logs. A managed workflow does not store the error, even for a `ServerlessError`. `job.error_message()` returns `{}`, and the exception that `job.result()` raises contains only the log lines that include `error` or `exception`. Checks of argument types and ranges belong in an [argument schema](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), which rejects a bad run before the job starts.\n"
msgstr "Saat workflow memunculkan exception, job berakhir dengan status `ERROR`, dan traceback masuk ke log. Managed workflow tidak menyimpan error tersebut, bahkan untuk `ServerlessError`. `job.error_message()` mengembalikan `{}`, dan exception yang dimunculkan `job.result()` hanya berisi baris log yang memuat `error` atau `exception`. Pemeriksaan tipe dan rentang argumen sebaiknya ada di [schema argumen](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#best-practice-validate-arguments-with-a-schema), yang menolak run yang salah sebelum job dimulai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report every error that stops the workflow with `send_error()`, so that your local notebook gets a short error with a code and details:\n"
msgstr "Laporkan setiap error yang menghentikan workflow dengan `send_error()`, supaya notebook lokalmu mendapat error singkat dengan kode dan detail:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException` with the same text.\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` memunculkan `QiskitServerlessException` dengan teks yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, raise `ServerlessError` where the error happens, and wrap the code of your entrypoint in a `try` block that sends any error with `send_error()`. A workflow adds this handler to Catalog Functions, but not to managed workflows:\n"
msgstr "Agar ini berfungsi, munculkan `ServerlessError` di tempat error terjadi, dan bungkus kode entrypoint-mu dalam blok `try` yang mengirim error apa pun dengan `send_error()`. Workflow menambahkan handler ini ke Catalog Functions, tetapi tidak ke managed workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Raise the error again.** The final `raise` keeps the traceback in the logs and ends the job with the `ERROR` status.\n"
msgstr "**Munculkan error itu lagi.** `raise` terakhir menjaga traceback di log dan mengakhiri job dengan status `ERROR`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Subclass `ServerlessError` to name a group of errors.** The handler sends the name of the class, such as `InputError`, as the `exception` field.\n"
msgstr "**Buat subclass `ServerlessError` untuk menamai sekelompok error.** Handler mengirim nama class, seperti `InputError`, sebagai field `exception`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other exceptions also reach the handler.** They get the code `1`, and their `repr()` becomes the message, such as `ValueError('bad shots')`.\n"
msgstr "**Exception lain juga sampai ke handler.** Exception itu mendapat kode `1`, dan `repr()`-nya menjadi pesan, seperti `ValueError('bad shots')`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: custom (user) workflows run their entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py (fleets_runner.py _upload_custom_image_entrypoint). Only provider jobs get the main.tmpl handler, which calls send_error() for an uncaught exception. Should custom jobs get the same handler? Tested with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0: a raised ServerlessError creates no ERROR event, and error_message() returns {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report a problem and continue {#report-a-problem-and-continue}"
msgstr "Laporkan masalah dan lanjutkan {#report-a-problem-and-continue}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`send_error()` does not stop the workflow or change its status, so you can also report problems that the workflow recovers from, such as each circuit that it skips:\n"
msgstr "`send_error()` tidak menghentikan workflow atau mengubah statusnya, jadi kamu juga bisa melaporkan masalah yang berhasil dipulihkan workflow, seperti setiap circuit yang dilewati:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns every error that the workflow reported, including the errors of a job that ended with the `DONE` status. See [Find the cause of an error](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-the-cause-of-an-error).\n"
msgstr "`job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` mengembalikan setiap error yang dilaporkan workflow, termasuk error dari job yang berakhir dengan status `DONE`. Lihat [Cari penyebab error](/guides/run-managed-workflow#find-the-cause-of-an-error).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pass numbers and strings in `args`.** `error_message()` shows only the first item of a list.\n"
msgstr "**Berikan angka dan string di `args`.** `error_message()` hanya menampilkan item pertama dari sebuah list.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Check the return value.** If a workflow cannot store the error, for example because the code runs outside a job, `send_error()` writes the error to the logs and returns `False`.\n"
msgstr "**Periksa nilai kembaliannya.** Kalau workflow tidak bisa menyimpan error, misalnya karena kode berjalan di luar job, `send_error()` menulis error ke log dan mengembalikan `False`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm which error codes user workflows should use. Catalog Function codes come from the IBM Quantum error code registry, which might not apply to user workflows. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clean up when a job is canceled {#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled}"
msgstr "Bersihkan saat job dibatalkan {#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When you cancel a job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint, uploads the final logs, and shuts down the environment. Without a handler, Python stops immediately, and `finally` blocks do not run. The workflow also tries to cancel the QPU jobs and sessions that the workflow started with `get_runtime_service()`. See [Cancel linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Saat kamu membatalkan job, workflow mengirim `SIGTERM` ke entrypoint-mu, mengunggah log terakhir, dan mematikan environment. Tanpa handler, Python langsung berhenti, dan blok `finally` tidak dijalankan. Workflow juga mencoba membatalkan job QPU dan session yang dimulai workflow dengan `get_runtime_service()`. Lihat [Batalkan job QPU yang terhubung](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep partial work, register a handler for `SIGTERM`. Your local notebook then gets the partial result from a canceled job:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menyimpan hasil parsial, daftarkan handler untuk `SIGTERM`. Notebook lokalmu kemudian mendapat hasil parsial dari job yang dibatalkan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, add the handler at the start of your entrypoint:\n"
msgstr "Agar ini berfungsi, tambahkan handler di awal entrypoint-mu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`sys.exit()` in the handler raises `SystemExit` in the code that is running, so `finally` blocks run before the script ends. The job still ends with the `CANCELED` status.\n"
msgstr "`sys.exit()` di handler memunculkan `SystemExit` di kode yang sedang berjalan, jadi blok `finally` dijalankan sebelum skrip berakhir. Job tetap berakhir dengan status `CANCELED`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the handler short, because the workflow shuts down the environment soon after `SIGTERM`. For long runs, also save checkpoints, so that a later run can resume after a job fails or reaches the 24-hour limit. See [Best practice: checkpoint long jobs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Buat handler tetap singkat, karena workflow mematikan environment tak lama setelah `SIGTERM`. Untuk run yang panjang, simpan juga checkpoint, supaya run berikutnya bisa dilanjutkan setelah job gagal atau mencapai batas 24 jam. Lihat [Praktik terbaik: beri checkpoint pada job panjang](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm the time between SIGTERM and shutdown. The cancel is a Code Engine hard stop (fleets/handler.py cancel_job, cancel_processing_tasks=True), and the repo sets no grace period. Tested with qiskit-serverless 0.37.0, the real fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py, and docker stop: the handler runs, save_result() writes the result, and result() on a CANCELED job returns it (the result endpoint does not check the status). Confirm on Fleets that a result written in the handler reaches storage before the hard stop. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah selanjutnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) to start a job and read its status, logs, and result.\n"
"- [Manage files across runs](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) to save checkpoints that a later run can resume from.\n"
"- [Choose a compute profile](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) to run your workflow with more CPU, memory, or GPU resources.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Rekomendasi\">\n"
"- [Jalankan managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) untuk memulai job dan membaca status, log, serta hasilnya.\n"
"- [Kelola file antar-run](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) untuk menyimpan checkpoint yang bisa dilanjutkan oleh run berikutnya.\n"
"- [Pilih compute profile](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles) untuk menjalankan workflow-mu dengan lebih banyak CPU, memori, atau sumber daya GPU.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
